{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia","id":1216486,"title":"Exigents in Autocthonia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-07T21:37:02-07:00","id":1216486,"title":"Exigents in Autocthonia","content":"Okay, I'll likely be dead before alchemicals 3E comes out. (Seriously, if we presume 2 years between fatsplats, it's likely the Alchemicals' won't show up until the 2030s(!). <br /> But in preparing for what is obviously the best Exalted type and setting in the universe. Has anyone thought about what the Autocthonian verison of exigents might be?<br /> <br /> God's don't play the same role in setting, so it'd likely be different, BUT.... We're talking the promordial of innovation here--so it's entirely likely new types of exalted, let's call them &quot;experimental exalts&quot; might appear now and then, especially if the Divine Ministers decide that the Five Nations need a hand. So what type of new Autobot exalts could <i>you</i> see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T22:03:59-07:00","id":1216493,"title":"","content":"Um...not to rain on your parade, but \u201cevery gods now has the ability to exalt people\u201d isn\u2019t a thing, since a god can only obtain an Exigent exaltation by petition for one, and only the Sun can give out one going by the book.<br /> <br /> And Autochthon doesn\u2019t get mentioned anywhere in the book as the creator of exaltation, so him creating some kind of new exalted \u201cSince he\u2019s the primordial of crafting\u201d is running on heavy second edition lore for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 05-08-2018, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T23:29:50-07:00","id":1216512,"title":"","content":"So the Exigence is a gift bestowed upon Celestial and Terrestrial gods by The Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> Since we don't have the UCS in Autobotonia, we would need to introduce that Autochthon has a way to similarly empower his gods to then empower humans. Just straigh cribbing the process would be a shortcut, and if you are just running a game set in Auto, it doesn't feel as cheap. But, if you want these to be considered in the greater scheme of things, I would suggest finding a way to differentiate the process. You could even ape the name of the new PCs from Trinity, the Inspired. I don't think you could take any other lore from them, but the name is a cute nod,<br /> <br /> It could also work the other way around, instead of Auto empowering a god to empower a human, maybe Auto guides mortals to arcane knowledge that allows them to take the power of a god. Could even lead to interesting religious debate, as these Inspired seem to buck the order of the Great Maker, but they are OF the Great Maker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T00:14:27-07:00","id":1216524,"title":"","content":"Autochthonia has no gods. Just the Divine ministers and some machine entities. And the ministers it seems have Adamant Caste Alchemicals instead of Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T04:48:11-07:00","id":1216573,"title":"","content":"Hmm, what was Somairot the god of again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T05:55:36-07:00","id":1216591,"title":"","content":"What if Autochonian Exigent Exaltations were like Alchemical Charms in that they are discreet things? I have the image of a cybernetic spinelike thing that attaches to a mortal (for life) and now they have access to its powers and charms. Something very comic book-like. As their power increases, more of their body becomes replaced with synthetic parts.<br /> <br /> Heck, I guess that would make the altered mortals in Keychain of Creation into kind of Autocthonian Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T06:25:21-07:00","id":1216606,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Autochthonia won't have exigents, 'cos there's no phone line to Conky. But not everything in the exigent book is gonna be an exigent. <br /> <br /> So I think diversifying the Autochthonia exalt population would be neat.<br /> <br /> Maybe you could have something like the &quot;Machine Blooded&quot;, basically dragon blooded but arranged around the Autochthonian elements.<br /> <br /> Or Augmented humans who resemble alchemicals from the modern shard or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T07:16:08-07:00","id":1216631,"title":"","content":"Because Autochthonia is already an almost entirely self-contained setting, I don't think there's anything very disruptive in the idea of a game in which Autochthon was able to provide a means for the subgods of his Divine Ministers to occasionally create their own Exalted in the same vein as Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T08:13:50-07:00","id":1216661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216573#post1216573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, what was Somairot the god of again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Extremely sad music.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T08:15:19-07:00","id":1216662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216661#post1216661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extremely sad music.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, little earthquakes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T09:10:38-07:00","id":1216695,"title":"","content":"I don't know who Tori Amos is!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T09:22:23-07:00","id":1216700,"title":"","content":"I could certainly imagine taking the Artifact and Evocation rules, sticking a mote pool on one of them, and then stapling it to a mortal's soul. Or having a god or elemental merge with a mortal and then the mortal has to deal with a passenger that can take over at times or something.<br /> <br /> Both of those seem like things that could create something similar to Exalted, but a bit more &quot;techy&quot; and with similar downsides to the sort of things you see in cyberpunk stories. Both could have enough downsides that someone's first reaction could be &quot;I didn't ask for this.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T10:00:38-07:00","id":1216716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216662#post1216662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, little earthquakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>*facepalm* I did not pick up on that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T10:35:20-07:00","id":1216731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216573#post1216573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, what was Somairot the god of again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring the stupid name joke that should never have seen print, she\u2019s in charge of probability modeling/revealing the future, making her a major patron of the Plutarchs. She\u2019s a subroutine of Kadmek.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T10:40:17-07:00","id":1216734,"title":"","content":"Anyway, it turns out that Somairot was just goddess of prophecy, with not much going for her besides an acrimonious relationship with Divine Minister Kadmek, owing to how he's also a deity of prophecy and has her as an assistant that he doesn't take very seriously. In particular, how their prognostications are bringing back different results on the question of the Octect trying to reach Creation, and him forbidding her from discussing her dissent with other spirits. <br /> <br /> \u200bEspinoquae, god of surveillance, light and security, seems like a stronger basis for developing an Exalt, with his focus on the acquisition and manipulation of intelligence, as well as his somewhat heterodox relationship with the Luminors. Hell, even the context given to him, where he's being given a workload going beyond his capabilities, might provide reason for him wanting or needing to create an Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T11:41:22-07:00","id":1216751,"title":"","content":"I'm working on fleshing out 7 Subroutines for each Divine Minister (+the Core) in the thread i have linked in my signature. It varies a bit from 2E canon (it works more like other Primordials' soul-structures, and less like the pseudo-animism of Creation, because while differing from other Primordials is fine, Autocthonia is more interesting in how it differs from Creation as a setting) but not by that much. I've posted Runel and Kek'tungsssha's Subroutines, and need to get back to it to post Debok Moom's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T15:40:08-07:00","id":1216832,"title":"","content":"If you'd like something that might work out like Exigents for Autochthonia, check out Masters of the Industrial Elements in my signature. Once I finish up other projects I'll be updating it to 3rd Edition, but the lore is still pretty solid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T21:16:33-07:00","id":1216892,"title":"","content":"What role would Autochthonian Exigents play? The usual niches are taken up by Alchemicals. Maybe guardians or leaders of communities outside the nations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T21:27:43-07:00","id":1216894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216734#post1216734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bEspinoquae, god of surveillance, light and security, seems like a stronger basis for developing an Exalt, with his focus on the acquisition and manipulation of intelligence, as well as his somewhat heterodox relationship with the Luminors. Hell, even the context given to him, where he's being given a workload going beyond his capabilities, might provide reason for him wanting or needing to create an Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem I'm having there, is there's a whole Caste of Alchemicals already dedicated to being secret agents for the Divine Ministers and their Subroutines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T21:32:25-07:00","id":1216895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216892#post1216892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What role would Autochthonian Exigents play? The usual niches are taken up by Alchemicals. Maybe guardians or leaders of communities outside the nations?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I can't imagine most Subroutines would care especially about said communities to make that level of commitment of their power, even if they had some equivalent of the flame of Exigence.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not saying there isn't room in Autochthonia for some other type of Exalted, but I don't think Exigents of the Ministerial Subroutines is a model fills a current vacuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T00:06:12-07:00","id":1216917,"title":"","content":"What I was getting at. The Nations use the 5 main Caste Alchemicals, Divine Ministets use Adamant (assuming that is still a thing this edition*).<br /> <br /> <br /> * which I hope it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T00:16:20-07:00","id":1216918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216917#post1216917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I was getting at. The Nations use the 5 main Caste Alchemicals, Divine Ministets use Adamant (assuming that is still a thing this edition*).<br /> <br /> <br /> * which I hope it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T00:44:23-07:00","id":1216921,"title":"","content":"Wasnt there a cyborg option in 2e? Where a auto.spirit would merge with a human? Not takling about gremlin syndrome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T00:47:17-07:00","id":1216922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216917#post1216917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I was getting at. The Nations use the 5 main Caste Alchemicals, Divine Ministets use Adamant (assuming that is still a thing this edition*).<br /> <br /> <br /> * which I hope it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and I was largely agreeing. I think if Autochthonia had another type of Exalted it would need a really distinct niche - neither being support for a mortal community (the role of the 5 Castes) or operatives of the Divine Ministers (Adamant). Or of course being champions of Autochthon's decay (Apostates).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T00:50:17-07:00","id":1216924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216921#post1216921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasnt there a cyborg option in 2e? Where a auto.spirit would merge with a human? Not takling about gremlin syndrome</div> </div> </div> </div>A Drone was a person possessed by a Machine Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T02:09:27-07:00","id":1216933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216894#post1216894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Problem I'm having there, is there's a whole Caste of Alchemicals already dedicated to being secret agents for the Divine Ministers and their Subroutines.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd there's a whole Caste of Solars dedicated to fighting off the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhere were they when Ten Sheathes saw the banners coming over the horizon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T02:13:16-07:00","id":1216934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216924#post1216924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Drone was a person possessed by a Machine Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank u. I would see drones as the auto. Equilavent to exigents. With the condition of Temporary volentary power which could leave at any moment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T04:01:28-07:00","id":1216942,"title":"","content":"hmm, I wonder if the nations could produce some sort of cyborg as well. a sort of pseudo machine-exigent...<br /> <br /> nah, too close too close to Alchemical half caste","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T02:20:42-07:00","id":1218159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1216942#post1216942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm, I wonder if the nations could produce some sort of cyborg as well. a sort of pseudo machine-exigent...<br /> <br /> nah, too close too close to Alchemical half caste</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking about that as a way to introduce the modern alchemicals, but you'd have to have some way to differentiate them from the traditional alchemicals-- perhaps a DB lifespan, and lesser powers, but with the change in how essence works, the simplest method (not allowing 5+ essence ratings) is no longer possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T03:28:33-07:00","id":1218163,"title":"","content":"thinking about that idea more, while I dont think the nations would have made charm using cyborgs before, just because Alchemicals would just be better, I could see a Twilight maybe who was familiar with Autochthonian tech developing something like that.<br /> <br /> Just an idea for what Solars could do once they start getting into Autochthonia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T04:03:50-07:00","id":1218168,"title":"","content":"One idea I had was based off altering the charm installation costs.<br /> <br /> Traditional alchemicals get slots but don't need to commit any motes, while modern types don't get slots but can manifest any charm in their library by committing personal motes (probably in some standardised way to keep things simple, like 1m for a caste/favoured and 2 for non-favoured or something)<br /> <br /> The fact that peripheral replenishes first means that modern alchemicals will still need downtime when they want to swap, because they'll need to de-commit their charms and wait for their pools to refill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T06:41:28-07:00","id":1218194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1218163#post1218163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thinking about that idea more, while I dont think the nations would have made charm using cyborgs before, just because Alchemicals would just be better, I could see a Twilight maybe who was familiar with Autochthonian tech developing something like that.<br /> <br /> Just an idea for what Solars could do once they start getting into Autochthonia</div> </div> </div> </div>The nationss not, but maybe small communities where one doesn't have that kind of material resources, someone in need - or with the right kind of sorcerous/thaumaturgical talent - might open oneself to be ridden by an agent of the machine god in expectation a form of help and/or enlightnement of sorts.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated aside, i ask myself how might alchemical charms interact and mesh (or not) with Evocations, what kind of weirdness this kind of interface could lead into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-13-2018, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:43:19-07:00","id":1218403,"title":"","content":"I had one thought for the Evocation based exalt in autocthon-- sort of a Tony Stark kind of character. More or less squishy by himself, but able ot build and create armor and equipment that is really incredible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:59:54-07:00","id":1218412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1218403#post1218403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had one thought for the Evocation based exalt in autocthon-- sort of a Tony Stark kind of character. More or less squishy by himself, but able ot build and create armor and equipment that is really incredible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd just make that character a Twilight. Unparalleled mastery of Evocations is already part of the Solar shtick. Remember Autochthonian mortals can start Exalting once the Seal is breached, which will immediately revolutionize Autochthonian society or throw it into complete disarray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T02:03:19-07:00","id":1218447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1218412#post1218412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd just make that character a Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the basic outline of this going to be the response to every suggested Exigent concept?<br /> <br /> &quot;Now why would you want to be the Chosen of Masks when you can be literally any other kind of Exalt and have access to all of your powers <i>all the time</i>?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T09:59:30-07:00","id":1218594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1218447#post1218447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the basic outline of this going to be the response to every suggested Exigent concept?<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Now why would you want to be the Chosen of Masks when you can be literally any other kind of Exalt and have access to all of your powers <i>all the time</i>?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Chosen of Masks is a very different concept than an evocation centered master of artificing. There are distinct concepts by design existing character types cover. I\u2019d hope a new type would get to do something they can\u2019t to that isn\u2019t distinctly covered by their place in the setting by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T10:09:09-07:00","id":1218597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1218594#post1218594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are distinct concepts by design existing character types cover. I\u2019d hope a new type would get to do something they can\u2019t to that isn\u2019t distinctly covered by their place in the setting by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<i>What?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T17:47:49-07:00","id":1219126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1218597#post1218597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b<i>What?</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exigents exist, extradiegetically speaking, to cover character concepts that aren't facilitated by other types of Exalted. A Tony Stark-esque master of evocations is 100% covered by an existing Exalted type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-15-2018, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T17:59:42-07:00","id":1219130,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Exigents would cover the Hulk and Spiderman. Tony Stark and Thor are Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T18:17:05-07:00","id":1219135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1219130#post1219130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Exigents would cover the Hulk and Spiderman. Tony Stark and Thor are Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Spiderman's a lunar-ish. Hulk might be an infernal? (Monster Mode, rage brawl, radiation?). I'd say Thor is more an exigent?<br /> <br /> But generally, in exalted, fictional characters could fit into more than one splat. I think Exigents fit the idea of a legacy hero a bit more than others do (Or rather can).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 05-15-2018, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T18:19:40-07:00","id":1219137,"title":"","content":"With any of these characters it depends entirely on what aspect you are choosing translate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T18:19:44-07:00","id":1219138,"title":"","content":"Gained his power by fucking up? <br /> <br /> Yeah, Hulk is pretty damn infernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T23:46:13-07:00","id":1219199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1219138#post1219138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gained his power by fucking up?<br /> <br /> Yeah, Hulk is pretty damn infernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, 2e Infernal; Vance has said he doesn't see spectacular failure as the defining criterion for 3e Infernal Exaltation, though it could lead to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T04:15:57-07:00","id":1219227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1219126#post1219126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Exigents exist, extradiegetically speaking, to cover character concepts that aren't facilitated by other types of Exalted. A Tony Stark-esque master of evocations is 100% covered by an existing Exalted type.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNo it isn't; not with quite that level of fidelity.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf Tony Stark is a Twilight Caste Solar Exalt, he can, and probably will, do things beyond the range of the armour. Even within consideration of how not all Solars explore all avenues of capability, he's still liable to have some Charms that take him away from the concept.<br /> <br /> \u200bSolars include exceptional medics as well, and yet Holden once gave a rather thorough breakdown of an Exigent focused on being a medic, including all of the ways that could differ from being a Solar.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe premise of &quot;this basic concept shouldn't be an Exigent because a Solar can do that&quot; <i>dramatically</i> reduced the number of viable Exigents, because Solars can actually do quite a few things. So I think your perspective on why they exist is off.<br /> <br /> Use Exigents to explore how the same character concept can be executed either with a different process, or a greater degree of fidelity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T06:18:44-07:00","id":1219251,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a twilight isn't iron man. A twilight is iron man welded to doctor strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T10:49:31-07:00","id":1219311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1219251#post1219251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, a twilight isn't iron man. A twilight is iron man welded to doctor strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>What aspect of Doctor Strange is represented in a Craft Supernal Solar whose player only takes Craft Charms and Evocations to represent being a brilliant artificer as the sole manifestation of the character\u2019s power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-16-2018, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T11:02:25-07:00","id":1219315,"title":"","content":"Well, a twilight will eventually need to learn sorcery to max out their crafting potential. I could see exigent Iron Man getting charms that circumvent that instead. They'd be way too powerful in the hands of a solar, but for a character capable of nothing else...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T11:14:32-07:00","id":1219322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1219311#post1219311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What aspect of Doctor Strange is represented in a Craft Supernal Solar whose player only takes Craft Charms and Evocations to represent being a brilliant artificer as the sole manifestation of the character\u2019s power?</div> </div> </div> </div>This strikes me as a bit like arguing that a Lunar can play Musashi, if they use their powerful attributes to wield a sword and never shapeshift. It's certainly true, but you have to deliberately neglect large parts of caste to make it work, so you're going pretty far from their &quot;default&quot; portrayal to do it.<br /> <br /> I also do have to say that part of the problem here is that Solar Craft is a bit flavorless. That said... to the extent that it has a flavor, a lot of it is closer to Strange. <i>Words as Workshop Method</i> is not something Iron Man can do. (Although I guess technically that's closer to <i>Green Lantern</i> thematics, if anything.)<br /> <br /> A more serious problem is that Iron Man is not a generic all-purpose super-crafter. Thematically, most of his power is invested in a single creation - one he's refined and revised and re-iterated on constantly, yes, but he's not Reed Richards or something. He makes his Iron Man suit and everything else is strictly secondary. That's not how Solar Craft works, and an Exigent focused on making and refining and reiterating on a single artifact might be a better fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-16-2018, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:40:05-07:00","id":1219391,"title":"","content":"A thought struck me as I was reading the more recent posts. <br /> <br /> What if the equivalent of exigents in Autochthonia took the form of a process that bonded a mortal with a single artifact. I'm thinking this would only work in Autochthonia due to Autochthon's connection to artifacts and 'tool use' in general. I feel it would also work best if it was a tradeoff for the mortal much like Gunzoasha armor. Perhaps similarly, it would drain the user's life force. Hmmmm... perhaps the process would bond the user's soul to the artifact in such a way that they are unable to be reincarnated afterwards, consumed by the bond. This would make the bond as rare or even rarer than exigents in creation.<br /> <br /> But these are desperate times for the 8 nations after all...<br /> <br /> These bonded mortals would perhaps treat evocations as native charms. Resonant with only their artifact they would perhaps be unable to even wield others? Of course, they wouldn't have access to any evocations gated off by the charms of another splat, but I feel like they'd gain some options from having a soul-deep bond with the artifact in question. <br /> <br /> Like exigents they could essentially fill any niche requirements without requiring the divine flame. They could even fill various power levels based on the artifact and dot rating of it. Their very existence could affect the evocation trees of Autochthonian artifacts after they die and their souls are trapped in the artifacts instead of being released into the Ewer. I'm thinking that the user would have their soul gem ritually removed and socketed into the hearthstone socket of the artifact as part of the bonding process perhaps. <br /> <br /> I dunno, It's just a thought, but what do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T13:50:05-07:00","id":1219398,"title":"","content":"The main thing worth considering with an Iron Man character is if being caught without their armour is actually compelling.<br /> <br /> This is a problem Alchemicals have had the last two editions, they talk a good game about having different load-outs but in reality there's a whole bunch of charms your typical PC would never want to let go of and try and players would try and argue their way around any obstacles to bringing them. Ever had an NPC try to get the PCs to relinquish their weapons? It's like that situation is baked into the splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T14:31:23-07:00","id":1219439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1219322#post1219322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">an Exigent focused on making and refining and reiterating on a single artifact might be a better fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMind, I feel as though this is the kind of thing in which the suit actually <i>is</i> the Exaltation, to which they become inextricably bonded, but that they can separate from (and need to in order to do things like modify Charm loadout).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T15:11:13-07:00","id":1219450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1219322#post1219322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This strikes me as a bit like arguing that a Lunar can play Musashi, if they use their powerful attributes to wield a sword and never shapeshift. It's certainly true, but you have to deliberately neglect large parts of caste to make it work, so you're going pretty far from their &quot;default&quot; portrayal to do it.<br /> <br /> I also do have to say that part of the problem here is that Solar Craft is a bit flavorless. That said... to the extent that it has a flavor, a lot of it is closer to Strange. <i>Words as Workshop Method</i> is not something Iron Man can do. (Although I guess technically that's closer to <i>Green Lantern</i> thematics, if anything.)<br /> <br /> A more serious problem is that Iron Man is not a generic all-purpose super-crafter. Thematically, most of his power is invested in a single creation - one he's refined and revised and re-iterated on constantly, yes, but he's not Reed Richards or something. He makes his Iron Man suit and everything else is strictly secondary. That's not how Solar Craft works, and an Exigent focused on making and refining and reiterating on a single artifact might be a better fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunar analogy doesn't translate IMO, because Lunars as we understand them (though admittedly we haven't seen them in 3E yet) have animal-shapeshifting rooted into their nature and charmset. If that doesn't fit the concept to some degree (though the exact degree can vary A LOT), it doesn't work as a Lunar. Like the Dragon-Blooded and the elements, Abyssals and death, and Sidereals and fate.<br /> <br /> In contrast, &quot;humans who in the context of their own narratives are 'just' super-skilled, but obviously superhuman compared to real human abilities&quot; are precisely one of the inspiring character types for Solars (not the only one obviously, it comes down to which Charms that player invests in to represent their vision of the character).<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Tony Stark only being about the one artifact, I've got a pile of graphic novels involving various inventions and super-science solutions to problems that say otherwise - so maybe it's the &quot;Tony Stark&quot; analogy that's throwing me off, and I could better understand Exigent concept in question with different examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T15:20:40-07:00","id":1219455,"title":"","content":"Do you not think something as basic and essential as a god of the forge could ever entail an Exigent?<br /> <br /> \u200bEspecially considering how Exigents are supposed to be about more than the conceptual purview, and actually account for the personality of the god?<br /> <br /> \u200bHow the novelty of mechanics such as the Chosen of a volcano god having Charms based around building up a kind of Pressure might imply methods of building Charms that would be distinct from Solars?<br /> <br /> \u200bGood Lord, the freaking Dragon Blooded now have an entirely different approach to Charms in the form of Elemental Keywords and the Aura mechanic that makes them play quite differently from the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bHey, here's another idea for a Tony Stark-like Exigent that would not be out of place in Autochthonia; all of their Charms serve as metaphorical components of things that they need to build (with a strong preference for a suite of personal enhancements, akin to something like the old raksha Assumptions), with the majority of Instant Charms being things that require the setup of having constructed an appropriate &quot;suit&quot; or &quot;gadget&quot; out of one's own Essence to facilitate their use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T16:04:27-07:00","id":1219466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1219455#post1219455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you not think something as basic and essential as a god of the forge could ever entail an Exigent?<br /> <br /> \u200bEspecially considering how Exigents are supposed to be about more than the conceptual purview, and actually account for the personality of the god?</div> </div> </div> </div>Intradiegetically of course any god can create an Exigent given access to the Exigence.<br /> <br /> Extradiegetically, I would ask the player what it is that want from the Exigent and their crafting that isn't done by craft-focused Exalted of existing types. Not only to determine if it's worth the work of designing a whole charmset for them, but also to know what themes to design said charmset around. If their answer is that they want to play a Tony Stark style master artificer who relies on Evocations, without anything more distinct power-wise than that, I'd tell them that Craft Supernal Twilights have them covered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bHow the novelty of mechanics such as the Chosen of a volcano god having Charms based around building up a kind of Pressure might imply methods of building Charms that would be distinct from Solars? </div> </div> </div>That's a perfect example of a niche that other Exalted types don't fill being filled by an Exigent.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hey, here's another idea for a Tony Stark-like Exigent that would not be out of place in Autochthonia; all of their Charms serve as metaphorical components of things that they need to build (with a strong preference for a suite of personal enhancements, akin to something like the old raksha Assumptions), with the majority of Instant Charms being things that require the setup of having constructed an appropriate &quot;suit&quot; or &quot;gadget&quot; out of one's own Essence to facilitate their use. </div> </div> </div>That is interesting and I'd like to hear more. I'm curious what their role would be in the Autochthonian setting. It interests me most of they're a new x-factor that represents a potential change/heresy, evolving away from traditional Autochthonia, as opposed to an additional support system playing the same role as Alchemicals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T01:47:34-07:00","id":1219561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1216486-exigents-in-autocthonia?p=1219450#post1219450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar analogy doesn't translate IMO, because Lunars as we understand them (though admittedly we haven't seen them in 3E yet) have animal-shapeshifting rooted into their nature and charmset. If that doesn't fit the concept to some degree (though the exact degree can vary A LOT), it doesn't work as a Lunar. Like the Dragon-Blooded and the elements, Abyssals and death, and Sidereals and fate.<br /> <br /> In contrast, &quot;humans who in the context of their own narratives are 'just' super-skilled, but obviously superhuman compared to real human abilities&quot; are precisely one of the inspiring character types for Solars (not the only one obviously, it comes down to which Charms that player invests in to represent their vision of the character).<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Tony Stark only being about the one artifact, I've got a pile of graphic novels involving various inventions and super-science solutions to problems that say otherwise - so maybe it's the &quot;Tony Stark&quot; analogy that's throwing me off, and I could better understand Exigent concept in question with different examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars (and their castes in particular) are more than just collections of abilities; your caste is as much about your goals and what you value as it is about what you do. The Twilight caste has a lengthy definition that Tony Stark only tangentially hits one note on. He'd have a huge amount of trouble hitting most of the Twilight Solar Experience bonuses with any regularity, say. He has no interest in mysticism, and he's not very focused on learning or knowledge for its own sake outside of his one talent. He would be a much better Dawn or Zenith with Craft favored; but he's a pretty terrible Twilight, since <i>learning stuff</i> is rarely the focus of an Iron Man story.<br /> <br /> (Whereas it's often the focus of a Doctor Strange story.)<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you couldn't make him as a Twilight, of course, since the castes are flexible. But he's absolutely not someone I'd point to as one of the caste's primary inspirations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T23:54:22-07:00","id":1220745,"title":"","content":"Well, given the current Earth-616 Iron Man is the powerful sorcerer and gifted technologist Victor von Doom . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T11:37:14-07:00","id":1220885,"title":"","content":"Victor von Doom, at least in the modern era, is probably the most Twilight character I can think of. I mean, there is even a Doom-bot charm, for better or for worse.<br /> <br /> Re: aping Raksha assumption/mutation charms, I've actually been ruminating about Raksha powers, rereading the 1st ed stuff, and it took this thread for me to realize that Alchemical charms and charmslots are a better implementation of Raksha assumption/mutation charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:18:50-07:00","id":1220917,"title":"","content":"Interesting topic. Re; the main thread and not the Marvel Comics stuff, I'll offer a contrasting point and offer that, I'm not sure Exigents, or any Exigent like Exalted *can* actually work in Autochthonia! (Without some pretty serious changes to assumptions, that is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> To explain, I think that it's pretty axiomatic to Autochthonia as a setting that the Alchemical Exalted are lifted up collective labour and technology, and are bound through that structure to service of the populace, rather than the internal cultivation of Essence and experience that empowers Creation's Exalted. Within Autochthonia, Exalted who deviate from this pattern are pretty renegade and strange and wrong, and that's a pretty important part of defining that setting.<br /> <br /> So I think it would be hard to introduce Exalted into that world who don't adhere to that structure, without undermining the feel of that setting and world. At least without acknowledging that you are actively disrupting the internal consistency of that setting, as would breaking the seal of the Eight Divinities.<br /> <br /> Then that leads to the question of whether you could broaden out the definition of Exalted-who-are-Alchemical-technological-golems to include Exalted with other Autochthonian patron deities. (Is there enough space there?)<br /> <br /> Yes, you certainly could! But I think in the process, you'd have to make Alchemicals much more &quot;of Autochthon&quot;. As it stands, Alchemicals, great as they are, seem to me not to have the flavour of Authochthon in the manner than Creation's Exalted have the flavour of their gods. They're much more Autochthonian in the manner of their construction and their material form, than in their Essence. Their Charms to me seem are material constructs and are not driven by a distinctive Essence of Autochthon in the way that Solar Charms are driven by the Essence of the Sun, or Dragonblooded Charms by the Five Elements.<br /> <br /> (Parenthetically, the Solars represent phases of the Sun's being; the Dragonblooded represent aspects of the Five Dragons. Each Alchemicals Caste represents and resonates most deeply with... one of the Five Magical Materials?).<br /> <br /> So to me I really think the question of Autochthonian parallels to Exigents is bound up with whether we want a space where Alchemicals stricto sensu, as the Exalted *of* Autochthon, are narrower and more defined as an elite Caste of the highest world-god, and we have a broad spectrum of Alchemical (in minds eye broadly bio-mechanical, without the body horror and with a dose of something brighter) Autochthonian Exalted of a variety of divine patrons within the Autochthonian environment. I think the Autochthonian setting could be a lot richer and its champions more defined for it, but, I'm not totally sure I'm the target audience!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 05-21-2018, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}